.\" File: man/femtofs.5
.\" Created by Andrea "Nemesi" Cocito on 08/11/2026
.\" FemtoFS resident-bank filesystem manual.
.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt FEMTOFS 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm femtofs
.Nd immutable resident-bank filesystem
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "kldload femtofs"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
kernel module mounts immutable images created by
.Xr makefemtofs 8 .
Images reside in named banks of wired RAM.
The boot loader can supply banks without a second full-image copy;
.Xr femtoctl 8
can import files or devices by copying their contents into RAM.
Mounts select a bank label, never a device pathname.
Labels contain 1 to 63 ASCII letters, digits, underscores or hyphens.
.Pp
Each bank permits one independent mount.
Unmounting releases mount caches but retains the bank and decoded metadata.
Discard unmounted banks with
.Xr femtoctl 8
before unloading the module.
Administration and mounting require root privileges, even when
.Va vfs.usermount
is enabled.
.Ss Mapping modes
The filesystem is always read-only.
Eligible memory mappings alias resident image pages.
Private writable mappings use copy-on-write and cannot change bank contents;
shared writable mappings are rejected.
The following mutually exclusive mount options select page-tail behavior:
.Bl -tag -width leaking
.It Cm clean
The default.
Pages requiring cleanup are copied lazily into a per-mount cache,
with bytes outside the file zero-filled.
.It Cm leaking
Allow mappings to expose adjacent public payload bytes in image pages.
Private payloads retain clean behavior.
Larger VM pages and active MAC policies force clean behavior.
.El
.Pp
Writable mounts, forced unmounts and asynchronous imports are unsupported.
.Ss Boot configuration
An example
.Pa /boot/loader.conf
configuration is:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
femtofs_load="YES"
root_load="YES"
root_type="femtofs_image"
root_name="/boot/root.0fs"
femtofs.bank.root="/boot/root.0fs"
vfs.root.mountfrom="femtofs:"
vfs.root.mountfrom.options="ro,clean,bank=root"
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Va femtofs.bank.
variables map labels to exact loader-recorded image names at module initialization.
Preload names must be unique and cannot be registered under multiple labels.
The distinct
.Cm femtofs_image
preload type avoids creating a writable md frontend.
Additional banks use additional label-to-image mappings.
.Pp
A read-only root requires
.Va root_rw_mount="NO"
in
.Pa /etc/rc.conf ,
writable storage for runtime state, and provisioned host identity and SSH keys.
Use fsck pass 0 in
.Pa /etc/fstab ;
for example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
root / femtofs ro,clean 0 0
.Ed
.Pp
The root mapping mode must agree with the loader options.
Alternatively, specify only
.Cm ro
in the root fstab entry.
.Ss Accounting
Read-only counters are available under
.Va vfs.femtofs :
.Bl -tag -width loader_released_pages
.It Va loader_bytes , imported_bytes
Retained allocation bytes by bank origin, including unmounted banks.
.It Va loader_image_bytes , imported_image_bytes
Logical image bytes by bank origin.
.It Va metadata_bytes
Decoded node and blob allocation bytes.
.It Va clean_bytes
Live wired clean-page cache bytes.
.It Va clean_pages
Clean pages populated since module load.
.It Va direct_faults , loader_faults
Pager faults aliasing bank pages: all origins and loader banks respectively.
.It Va loader_released_pages
Preload pages passed to stock reclamation since module load.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /boot/modules/femtofs.ko
.It Pa /boot/modules/femtofs.ko
Installed kernel module.
.It Pa /dev/femtofs
Administrator-only bank-control endpoint; not an image device.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr femtoctl 8 ,
.Xr kldload 8 ,
.Xr makefemtofs 8 ,
.Xr mount_femtofs 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh NOTES
The current native target is FreeBSD 15.1 amd64.
Revision 0x0101 uses the image creation time for every vnode timestamp,
with seconds measured from January 1, 2017 UTC.
Revision 0x0100 uses Unix-epoch timestamps.
Per-file chronology is not stored.
.Pp
Image hashes detect accidental corruption; they do not authenticate images.
Validate the source's authenticity separately.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Andrea "Nemesi" Cocito
.\" END File: man/femtofs.5
